<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8c5c69f7f7a7295b315885d5090de4a97c54d166" commit="470be13de94988ffdcfd15a63feae6c37417981f" commit_message="Add support for continuous SPI reads  This patch adds support for &quot;unbounded reads&quot; which are for continous reads to a SPI flash chip instead of reading in page size blocks.  This speeds up the flash process over FTDI by quite a bit, testing the read of a 16MB part it goes from 2m11s to 0m15s.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46914 BRANCH=none TEST=test flash read with and without the patch via servo and in-system to ensure that the data is read the same in both cases.  Change-Id: I8c5c69f7f7a7295b315885d5090de4a97c54d166 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308961 Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308961" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/61/308961/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4c203d29208618f533d16ac149a6f641ef3d0e2d" commit="f17a8ab8fd6d192c9e5add652dfd4dd5e1ee2d9f" commit_message="W25Q128: Enable unbounded read support  This patch enables the unbounded read feature on W25Q128.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46914 BRANCH=none TEST=test flash read with and without the patch via servo and in-system to ensure that the data is read the same in both cases.  Change-Id: I4c203d29208618f533d16ac149a6f641ef3d0e2d Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308962 Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308962" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/62/308962/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If01f6c8654dedb4b964cb31d589660f4a2cb61c0" commit="617b6240fa1ee23781c25be7ccd49a685e18df6a" commit_message="Fix duplicated GUID error when making universal factory shim.  We made a change previously to preserve partition GUID in make_universal_factory_shim.sh for merge_factory_usbimg.sh. However, when generating RMA images via make_universal_factory_shim.sh, it will have &quot;Duplicated GUID&quot; error if the factory test image version and release image version are the same.  Fixing this by using an environment variable to determine whether to preserve GUID or not.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:36725 CQ-DEPEND=CL:273100 TEST=1. make_universal_factory_shim.sh -f -m usbimg1.bin universal_usbimg.bin usbimg1.bin usbimg2.bin      2. merge_factory_usbimg.sh -f output.bin usbimg1.bin      Checks that GUIDs are *NOT* preserved in 1. but are preserved in 2.  Change-Id: If01f6c8654dedb4b964cb31d589660f4a2cb61c0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308302 Commit-Ready: Bowgo Tsai &lt;bowgotsai@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bowgo Tsai &lt;bowgotsai@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308302" owner_email="bowgotsai@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/02/308302/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If60d1839799dfbcab0d45c02bb8367c27c9e28f4" commit="d214d12d75424c96c1e8d5de4b0f3c287c6e979e" commit_message="HACK: soc/tegra: pmc: Ungate DFD partition across suspend/resume  There are some systems which will always hang at resume time that, for some reason, can be brought back to life be leaving the DFD partition ungated.  Leave DFD ungated across suspend/resume until we figure out the root cause of these hangs.  A possible side-effect from this is a very slight increase in power consumption.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46608 TEST=Suspend/resume now works on affected systems.  Change-Id: If60d1839799dfbcab0d45c02bb8367c27c9e28f4 Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308622 Reviewed-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308622" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/22/308622/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I4a065de0f4045a01bef1dc9fbb2e0578b5508518" commit="b0cffbd32f1888d30291bec5dec0388f3e3565d1" commit_message="libpayload: Fix building dwc2 UDC driver  Change Ie54699162 changed a structure's name and field names and we didn't notice. Adapt.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=building with UDC_DWC2 works  Change-Id: I4a065de0f4045a01bef1dc9fbb2e0578b5508518 Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308791 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308791" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/91/308791/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iff1d68f095fcd47eaca1a4c037c477a25ae2c7a7" commit="3450b31e787bb50579aea698dd479d94effdff0e" commit_message="drm/nouveau: pmu: Change the init value of elpg_disable_depth to 1  ELPG will be enabled by default when GPMU finishes booting, which means refcount &quot;elpg_disable_depth&quot; will get decreased by 1. So to keep this counter to 0 when nobody enable/disable ELPG, set it's initial value to 1.  Also this patch removes the codes in pmu's .fini function, to set &quot;elpg_disable_depth&quot; to 0. This doesn't make much sense because &quot;elpg_disable_depth&quot; will be set to 1 in .init later.  BUG=none TEST=Boots to UI OK  Change-Id: Iff1d68f095fcd47eaca1a4c037c477a25ae2c7a7 Signed-off-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305621 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305621" owner_email="markz@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/305621/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I23b859690509222ab92c09d37cf1bdbc582113e4" commit="c9e60f1f60d4fab863c28e3866809022d83e5737" commit_message="Revert &quot;Revert rt5677 hotwording support&quot;  This is a reland of hotwording support on rt5677. In a previous commit we changed that GPIO_CTRL1 and GPIO_CTRL2 registers can be configured as volatile using dtsi config, which fixes the original issue that speaker amp and dmic enable pin being reset across suspend/resume.  This reverts commit 9abbf21f14b12242e12d503d455765ace39e87ae.  BUG=b:24334115 TEST=Update kernel to Smaug, verify hotwording works.  Change-Id: I23b859690509222ab92c09d37cf1bdbc582113e4 Signed-off-by: Hsin-Yu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307663 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Anatol Pomazau &lt;anatol@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307663" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/63/307663/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I430d9b9a6b9987825459689d512d9bba46d2d4bb" commit="8d0ec158b63f02c33d9b8aa3542770f85f3fd1e8" commit_message="Remove toolchain-major builder.  The compiler branch this builder is using is not being maintained. Does not make sense to try to build this for now.  BUG=chromium:538675 TEST=run_tests  Change-Id: I430d9b9a6b9987825459689d512d9bba46d2d4bb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308752 Commit-Ready: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Han Shen &lt;shenhan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308752" owner_email="llozano@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/52/308752/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I2a7e9bf278bd37919176c09631b8560d08630a95" commit="9b9e7ac297942a7ce3a4bba86fc85fe90172f254" commit_message="Revert &quot;FROMLIST: PM / sleep: Go direct_complete if driver has no callbacks&quot;  This reverts commit f3e3ccd232458b637d7b65394bcecd81e021cd3e.  There is a recursive spinlock bug introduced in this change, so revert until it's fixed upstream.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46894 TEST=boot oak  Change-Id: I2a7e9bf278bd37919176c09631b8560d08630a95 Signed-off-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308997 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308997" owner_email="dbasehore@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/97/308997/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3a14a75fb15f9142323757579985cd49da5720bc" commit="64fe36631843c2865c1b2ab19c267117583ed0bb" commit_message="CHROMIUM: clk: tegra: dfll: fix logic for building lookup table  The lookup table entries are fixed, and the voltages in these entries are distributed based on minimum and maximum voltages and each voltages in opp table.  Since the last entry is reserved for maximum voltage, we found the voltage in the next to last entry is not accurate enough for the next to last frequency in some SKUs. This causes the DFLL driver cannot find a proper voltage index when CPUFreq driver set expected frequency as the next to last frequency.  This patch fixes the original logic to force to use find_vdd_map_entry_exact() for the next to last frequency, this will make the selected voltage are more accurate.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46846 TEST=Boots on smaug, check if the kernel log and no below errors:  [   95.945181] tegra124-dfll 70110000.clock: dfll_calculate_rate_request: Rate 18446744073709551594 is above dfll range [   96.178318] tegra124-dfll 70110000.clock: dfll_calculate_rate_request: Rate 4294967294 is above dfll range [   96.187973] tegra-dvfs: rate 18446744073709551594 too high for dvfs on cclk_g  Change-Id: I3a14a75fb15f9142323757579985cd49da5720bc Signed-off-by: Penny Chiu &lt;pchiu@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308281 Commit-Ready: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Huang &lt;bilhuang@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308281" owner_email="pchiu@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/308281/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8e9949b3ca9f6e766310e6765574fbbeba1444f5" commit="8572577e6e53cd396834049699c8e70af54c179e" commit_message="overlord: fix racing condition  Go 1.4 enable multi-threaded by default. Add mutex around shared resource to avoid racing condition.  BUG=none TEST=`for i in $(seq 1000); do         ghost --no-rpc-server --no-lan-disc --rand-mid       done`  Change-Id: I8e9949b3ca9f6e766310e6765574fbbeba1444f5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308341 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308341" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/41/308341/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I942b37affc7248a74ee6fd08eb8acef915803dd2" commit="b7f11897c532b54647f098c921489e9505e4bac8" commit_message="Add pressure calibration for Jerry's Synaptics TP  Jerry is getting a second-sourced touchpad from Synaptics.  The FW just went in, so this is a pressure calibration for it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45293 TEST=manually tested and deployed on a Synaptics Jerry  Change-Id: I942b37affc7248a74ee6fd08eb8acef915803dd2 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308964 Reviewed-by: Dennis Kempin &lt;denniskempin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="308964" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/xorg-conf" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/xorg-conf" ref="refs/changes/64/308964/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I62acca11890b8e33470da0d72a9249813d8ea18d" commit="cd304eb95c7b05bc175262b4b5f37659e6af5ad0" commit_message="Lars/Chell: add boards to chromeos-bootimage  BUG=None TEST=emerge-lars chromeos-bootimage  Change-Id: I62acca11890b8e33470da0d72a9249813d8ea18d Signed-off-by: David Wu &lt;David_Wu@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308680 Commit-Ready: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Tested-by: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="308680" owner_email="david_wu@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/80/308680/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I52b172273b53e8482b3f39024625ac6379cca61c" commit="757e75774dd6b6752411711af5c86023e81ba334" commit_message="Add 1080p video test to video_VideoEncodeAccelerator.  The capabilities of some codec can encode 1080p videos. Add 1080p video to test against the spec.  BUG=chromium:532771 TEST=Run the test on peach pi.  Change-Id: I52b172273b53e8482b3f39024625ac6379cca61c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308730 Commit-Ready: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="308730" owner_email="wuchengli@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/30/308730/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I586ba3e4349929782e734af1590f394824e7dd44" commit="1ddd796cba3a584641eef317ea3a29b3260bc233" commit_message="sign_official_build: add support for signing standalone accessories  Use futility to re-sign standalone accessory firmware images either the former &quot;usbpd1&quot; used by USB Power Delivery firmware generated from the EC codebase or the new &quot;rwsig&quot; format.  BRANCH=smaug, samus BUG=chrome-os-partner:46635 TEST=manual: openssl genrsa -F4 -out key_zinger.pem 2048 openssl genrsa -F4 -out key_hadoken.pem 2048 futility create --desc=&quot;Hadoken fake MP key&quot; key_hadoken.pem key_hadoken ./scripts/image_signing/sign_official_build.sh accessory_usbpd build/zinger/ec.bin . build/zinger/ec.SIGNED.bin ./scripts/image_signing/sign_official_build.sh accessory_rwsig build/hadoken/keyboard_app.bin . build/hadoken/keyboard_app.SIGNED.bin and compare the re-signed files with the original files.  Change-Id: I586ba3e4349929782e734af1590f394824e7dd44 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/306795 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="306795" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/95/306795/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="7587.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>